puller: flush semaphore words on the split's back thread

ReadSemaphoreWord flushed a GPU-written semaphore word out of the buffer cache
on the front. FlushRegion downloads through the Vulkan scheduler, which the back
owns even after a drain: its idle hook (FlushDeferred -> DispatchWork) can run
then, and the scheduler's chunk is empty for a moment. That is the same race as
the ReleaseFences crash 0041 fixed. The flush now runs on the back, and the front
waits for it with the drain its callers already did, so semaphore acquires gain
no round trip. The acquire path also releases the pending fences without a
drain of their own: ReadSemaphoreWord's drain waits for them, and the word is
read before Latched is checked.

